# Redirects from the old Webador site.
#
# Cloudflare reads this file at deploy time; it is never served as a page.
# Format: old path, new path, status. 301 means "moved for good", which tells
# Google to move the old page's standing to the new one and lets browsers
# remember the move.
#
# The full list of old addresses, and why each one goes where it does, is in
# docs/old-site-urls.md. Change one, change the other.
#
# Not listed: /, /contact, /pub-runs and /our-races. The new site has pages at
# exactly those addresses, so old links to them already work. Don't add them
# here — a rule always wins over a real page, and a rule pointing a page at
# itself is a loop.
#
# Destinations end in a slash because that is the address each page really
# lives at. Without it, the visitor gets this redirect and then a second one
# from Cloudflare adding the slash.
#
# Each old path is listed twice, with and without a trailing slash, because a
# rule only matches the exact path written.

/race-calendar                                /calendar/                 301
/race-calendar/                               /calendar/                 301
/boring-legal-stuff/rules-and-constitution    /rules-and-constitution/   301
/boring-legal-stuff/rules-and-constitution/   /rules-and-constitution/   301

